L001999	\ssec{Potential for dark siren cosmology}
L002000	\Acp{CBC} act as dark sirens providing constraints on their source distances; cross-referencing the inferred localization volume with galaxy catalogs that provide redshift information then enables inference of the Hubble constant~\cite{Schutz:1986gp,Gair:2022zsa,LIGOScientific:2025jau}.
L002001	Localization of \ac{GW} sources is best for high-\ac{SNR} signals observed with at least three detectors~\cite{Abbott:2020qfu,DelPozzo:2018dpu,Pankow:2019oxl,Emma:2024mjs,Ouzriat:2025ben}.
L002002	
L002003	Since the two signals have well-localized sources, they could be considered as potentially useful dark sirens.
L002004	Unfortunately, \ac{GW240925} will not provide significant cosmological information from its localization as it is hidden by the Milky Way plane.
L002005	However, \ac{GW250207} has a localization volume of $\sim\gwFebVol~\mathrm{Mpc}^3$, similar to that of \acsu{GW190814} ($\sim \gwAugVol~\mathrm{Mpc}^3$~\cite{Abbott:2020khf,LIGOScientific:2021usb}), far from the Milky Way plane, making it well suited for a dark siren cosmological analysis.
L002006	The host galaxy of \ac{GW250207} has an estimated probability $\sim\gwFebGLADEfraction$ to be present in the \ac{GLADEplus} catalog~\cite{Dalya:2018cnd,Dalya:2021ewn}.
L002007	This probability is based on the K-band luminosity, assumes that the likelihood of hosting a \ac{CBC} is proportional to the galaxy luminosity, and adopts a flat cosmological model with $\HzeroSymbol = \PlanckHubble~\mathrm{km\,s^{-1}\,Mpc^{-1}}$ and $\WmSymbol = \PlanckOmegaM$~\cite{Ade:2015xua,LIGOScientific:2025yae}.
L002008	Both signals will be included in a comprehensive analysis of all detections up to the end of \ac{O4}, which will be presented with a future version of the \ac{GWTC}, similar to the analysis for \ac{GWTC}-4.0~\cite{LIGOScientific:2025jau}.
L002009	This population analysis will allow information from multiple detections to be combined with a proper computation of selection effects across observing runs.
L002010	===== END FILE: source/5-cosmology.tex =====
L002011	
